  "concept": "OFFLINE REFERENCE — Two garden courts separate parallel two-storey wings, joined by an inhabited stair bridge. Continuous internal galleries connect the rooms without passing through bedrooms. The aligned upper bridge connects the private wings. A one-storey east library volume touches the ground wing and stays absent on the upper floor. This independently authored H arrangement proves articulated massing and stack fidelity, not generated design quality.",
